{
 "about": "Crafting, as the OSRS Wiki's item pages give it (read 2026-10-30). spinning: what a spinning wheel spins, in the Make-X box's order, with the level and XP in tenths; 3 ticks each (Ball of wool and Bow string pages), the first 2 ticks after the choice inferred from fletching's 'Make-X is 2, then 3 ticks'. The wheels are every loc the cache names Spinning wheel with a Spin option. anim 466 is the cache's 'spinningwheel' seq, taken to be the player's (inferred from the name; the wheels have no animation of their own). leather: a needle on leather, hard leather or dragon leather opens the Make-X box over what it makes, with how many leathers each takes (Leather, Hardleather body, Green dragon leather and the d'hide pages); thread is held and one is used up every 5 items (Thread: 'Each thread spool has 5 uses before it is consumed'). 3 ticks an item, hard leather 2 (each item's page); the first 2 ticks after the choice is inferred as for spinning. The Wiki gives leather boots 16.3 XP (16.25 elsewhere): 163 tenths. anim 1249 is human_leather_crafting. studs: steel studs on a leather body or chaps, 3 ticks (Studded body). Out: d'hide shields (they need a maple shield and nails), snakeskin, spiky vambraces and the costume needle. gems: a chisel on each uncut gem, 2 ticks a gem (each gem's page; the first 2 ticks after the choice inferred), with the cache's cutting animation for each. Opal, jade and red topaz can be crushed: crush gives the success pair out of 256 (SuccessRoll) worked back from each page's formula, (level-1)*122/98+129 for opal, *145/98+101 for jade and *150/98+91 for red topaz, all over 256, and the XP a crushed gemstone gives (3.8, 5 and 6.3). Out: the jeweller's chisel and amethyst. jewellery: a gold bar or a mould used on a furnace opens crafting_gold (interface 446), which lays itself out from the inventory; each item button (its component in 446) makes the item from a gold bar and its gem, with its mould held: levels and XP from the Wiki's Jewellery page, 3 ticks each (Gold ring), anim 899 human_furnace (guessed from smelting), the first 2 ticks after the click inferred. Bracelets use the real items, not the interface's dummies. amuletStringing: a ball of wool on an unstrung amulet, level 1, 4 XP, 2 ticks (Gold amulet). A silver bar or a silver mould on a furnace opens silver_crafting (interface 6) the same way: opal, jade and topaz jewellery, the unstrung holy symbol and unholy symbol, the silver sickle and the tiara (Silver bar's Products table; the ticks, animation and stringing XP taken to be gold's, inferred). A shared mould on a furnace opens the silver one only when the player holds a silver bar and no gold bar (guessed). Out: the slayer ring, the lightning rod, silver bolts, the Silvthrill rod and the demonic sigil (quest or crossbow items), stringing symbols, enchanting. glass: soda ash or a bucket of sand used on a furnace makes molten glass from one of each, leaving the bucket (Molten glass: level 1, 20 XP, 2 ticks; the furnace animation guessed); a glassblowing pipe on molten glass opens the Make-X box over the blown items (Glassblowing pipe for levels and XP, Vial for 3 ticks, the others taken to match; anim 884 human_glassblowing). pottery: soft clay on a potter's wheel, or its Use, shapes the unfired items (3 ticks, Unfired pie dish; anim 883 human_potterywheel); an unfired item on a pottery oven, or its Fire, fires it (7 ticks, any level: the oven pages), cracking now and then until level 13 (levels and both XPs from the Crafting page's Pottery table): every item's chart is the same, which the 180, 800 pair gives exactly (CraftingDataTest); a cracked piece is lost with no XP (guessed), and the oven animation is guessed. softClay: water from a bucket, jug, vial or bowl on clay softens it, giving the container back (Soft clay: 2 ticks, no XP). Ids are the 241 cache's; names are its gamevals.",
